- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vulnerable Ethiopians to Benefit from $745 Million in Grants for Improved Access to Health Services and Flood Management Projects","publisher":"World Bank","publication_date":"2022-12-13","url":"https://www.worldbank.org/en/news/press-release/2022/12/14/vulnerable-ethiopians-to-benefit-from-745-million-in-grants-for-improved-access-to-health-services-and-flood-management","claim":"The World Bank approved two grants for Ethiopia: one to improve equitable health services nationwide, including in conflict-affected areas and for women and children, and one to strengthen flood management, disaster resilience, and early warning systems for poor communities.","locator":"lines 24-35","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary World Bank press release with exact amounts, target populations, and implementation design.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"This is government-facing support under Abiy's administration; it is stronger evidence of spending priorities than of personal management quality.","contrary_evidence":["The projects are compensating for severe conflict and climate damage rather than showing a fully healthy economy.","The press release itself emphasizes the recent disruption of services and livelihoods."],"lenses":["5B.6","5B.8","5B.10"]}
